# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 vecteur.cc mmult_atranb, under every product of two matrices (operator* of two _VECT, mmult, mmultck): when neither factor holds doubles only (mmult_double), the product of a sparse pair (matrix_density(a)*matrix_density(btran) <= 0.1) runs a loop over the left factor's entries that skips each entry with is_zero(acur,context0), and matrix_density counts zeros with is_zero too. is_zero of a float compares it with epsilon, an absolute 1e-12 at any Digits (gen.cc is_zero: an MPFR value's double), so above Digits 14 a left factor whose entries are all below 1e-12 counted as empty and every entry was skipped: approx([[10^-13,0],[0,10^-13]])*[[1,2],[3,4]] = [[0,0],[0,0]] at Digits 40 (right [[1E-13,2E-13],[3E-13,4E-13]]), approx([[10^-13,10^-13],[0,10^-13]])*approx([[1,2],[3,4]]) = [[0,0],[0,0]] (right [[4E-13,6E-13],[3E-13,4E-13]]), approx([[10^-13,0],[0,10^-13]])*approx([[10^-13,0],[0,10^-13]]) = [[0,0],[0,0]] (right [[1E-26,0],[0,1E-26]]), and evalf([[10^-19,0],[0,10^-19]])*evalf([[1,0],[0,1]]) (met by G554); a small right factor, one left entry above 1e-12 (dense loop) and doubles at Digits 12 (mmult_double) were right. Now both tests ask for an exact zero (is_exactly_zero): an exact 0, or a float whose value is 0. The sparse loop and the choice between the loops are otherwise unchanged; is_zero and epsilon are not changed.
